   "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix: the honorific prefix sits BEFORE the base and the closed op enum has no prepend operation, so no ordered sequence reaches the surface. The suffixal half on its own (masu-stem + ください) would emit *待ちください instead of お待ちください. The record also makes the prefix lexically selected rather than derivable from the base token (お + masu-stem for native verbs, ご + verbal noun for Sino-Japanese suru-verbs: ご注意ください), and it excludes monosyllabic-stem verbs such as 見る from the pattern."
  },
  {
   "slug": "gram:o-ni-naru",
   "nuance_tags": [
    "honorific",
    "politeness"
   ],
   "usage_contexts": [
    "spoken",
    "business",
    "announcement"
   ],
   "steps_unavailable": "Circumfix: お / ご stands BEFORE the base and the closed op enum has no prepend operation. The suffixal half alone (masu-stem + になる) would emit *読みになる instead of お読みになる, and the お vs ご choice follows the base's native/Sino-Japanese origin (ご利用になる), which is not derivable from the token. The record further states that 見る, 来る and する take suppletive honorifics (ご覧になる, いらっしゃる, なさる), so any verb-wide rule would license *お見になる."
  },
